<title>UK: LVMH SELLS TWO MLN MORE GUINNESS SHARES.</title>
<headline>LVMH SELLS TWO MLN MORE GUINNESS SHARES.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-08-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Guinness Plc said on Thursday that LVMH Moet Hennessy Louis Vuitton sold two million Guinness shares on Wednesday at 591p per share, leaving the French luxury goods and drinks group with an 11.99 percent stake in the British firm.</p>
<p>Bernard Arnault, chairman of LVMH, opposes the proposed 24 billion stg merger between Guinness and Grand Metropolitan Plc and has been reducing his stake in Guinnes from 14.2 percent to build a holding in Grandmet.</p>
<p>Arnault's 11.06 percent Grandmet stake and his holding in Guinness allow him to call extraordinary meetings of both firms. He can block the deal outright if he can form an investor alliance representing at least 25 percent of Grandmet's share capital.</p>
<p>--London Newsroom +44 171 542 4019</p>
</text>
